@startuml SequenceReturn
actor Staff
participant ":LibraryRenderer" as UI
participant ":CirculationController" as Controller
participant ":Catalog" as Catalog
participant "copy:Copy" as Copy
participant "loan:Loan" as Loan
participant ":LibrarySettings" as Settings
participant "fine:Fine" as Fine
participant "book:Book (Subject)" as Book
participant "next:Reservation" as Reservation
participant ":HoldNotifier (HoldObserver)" as Observer
participant "student:Student" as Student
participant ":EmailAdapter (NotificationSender)" as Adapter
participant ":EmailService" as Service
note over UI,Service
Controller workflow on the stacked branch.
Catalog, Copy, Book, Reservation, Student and Observer classes are pending.
Loan.createFine currently returns undefined; fine construction below is an owner contract.
Book subscriptions are established during wiring, before this use case.
end note
Staff -> UI: scan return
UI -> Controller: returnCopy(barcode)
Controller -> Catalog: findCopy(barcode)
Catalog --> Controller: copy
alt copy missing
    Controller --> UI: null
else copy found
    Controller -> Copy: currentLoan()
    Copy --> Controller: loan
    alt no loan or already returned
        Controller --> UI: null
    else open loan
        Controller -> Loan: isOverdue(today)
        Loan --> Controller: late
        opt late
            Controller -> Loan: daysLate(today)
            Loan --> Controller: days
            Controller -> Settings: calculateFine(days)
            Settings --> Controller: amount
            Controller -> Loan: createFine(amount)
            note over Loan,Fine: Required owner implementation: attach new Fine(amount) and return it
            Loan --> Controller: fine (currently undefined)
        end
        alt late and no fine
            Controller --> UI: throws integration error
            note over Copy,Loan: Loan stays open; no hold assignment or notification
        else on time or fine created
            Controller -> Loan: close(today)
            Controller -> Copy: getBook()
            Copy --> Controller: book
            Controller -> Book: nextReservation()
            Book --> Controller: next
            opt next exists
                Controller -> Settings: calculateHoldDueDate(today)
                Settings --> Controller: holdDueDate
                Controller -> Reservation: hold(holdDueDate, copy)
                Reservation --> Controller: false if refused; void if assigned
                opt hold succeeded
                    Controller -> Book: notify(next)
                    loop subscribed HoldObservers (pending contract)
                        Book -> Observer: notify(next)
                        Observer -> Reservation: getStudent()
                        Reservation --> Observer: student
                        Observer -> Student: getEmail()
                        Student --> Observer: email
                        Observer -> Adapter: sendTo(email, message)
                        Adapter -> Service: deliver({recipients: [email], subject, body})
                    end
                end
            end
            Controller --> UI: Fine or null (on time)
        end
    end
end
note over UI: Distinguish refused from on-time null by inspecting the loan state.
Show an integration failure if an error is thrown.
@enduml
